derivations.claim:
The Poisson kernel. Dotting step 4.1 with $
u(y)=(y-a)/R$ from [F4] gives $\partial_{
u_y}G(x,y)=- rac{(R^2-|x-a|^2)(y-a)\cdot(y-a)}{\omega_{n-1}R^3|x-y|^n}=- rac{R^2-|x-a|^2}{R\omega_{n-1}|x-y|^n}$, because $(y-a)\cdot(y-a)=R^2$; hence by [F2], $P_{R,a}(x,y)=-\partial_{
u_y}G(x,y)=(R^2-|x-a|^2)/(R\omega_{n-1}|x-y|^n)$ for $x
e a$.
